  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 0.647, g: 0.678, b: 0.729, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '<b>[SECTION DESCRIPTION]</b>



    Both zones Respond To: <b>Tap</b>.
    They differ only in <b>Detect Outside</b>.



    Each zone holds <b>two boxes</b>,
    so "inside" means either one and "outside" means neither.



    <b>Left, Detect
    Outside off</b> - tap either grey box and the knob flashes green. Tap anywhere
    else and nothing happens.



    <b>Right, Detect Outside ON</b> - the knob flashes
    for everything EXCEPT its two boxes.



    <b>Note:</b> a zone spans the whole
    screen, not its half of the layout. Tapping the LEFT boxes also fires the RIGHT
    knob, because they are outside it. That is correct.



    Drags are ignored
    by both zones.

'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
